From c70febf2c3c197070bfbf4bb40caae09481a5879 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:57:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 73/74] Sample reader: no access to address 0 when no cache is
 written

readSamplesResampled() read *cacheWritePos at its start; with a null cacheWritePos (no cache written) that read address
0, and the compiler then dropped the null check at the end and wrote the value back to address 0 (found by the retune
tests in the emulator, 790 writes in 4 bars with stretched and resampled voices). Read it only when it's there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
---
 src/deluge/model/sample/sample_low_level_reader.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/model/sample/sample_low_level_reader.cpp b/src/deluge/model/sample/sample_low_level_reader.cpp
index 541f55c6..eea12144 100644
--- a/src/deluge/model/sample/sample_low_level_reader.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/model/sample/sample_low_level_reader.cpp
@@ -1002,7 +1002,9 @@ void SampleLowLevelReader::readSamplesResampled(int32_t** __restrict__ oscBuffer
 
 	int32_t* __restrict__ oscBufferPosNow = *oscBufferPos;
 
-	char* __restrict__ cacheWritePosNow = (char*)*cacheWritePos;
+	// Null when no cache is written: read only then, so the check at the end isn't optimised away (it wrote to address
+	// 0)
+	char* __restrict__ cacheWritePosNow = cacheWritePos ? (char*)*cacheWritePos : nullptr;
 
 	int32_t const* const oscBufferEnd = oscBufferPosNow + numSamplesTotal * numChannelsAfterCondensing;
 
